1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,978
This is The Organized Mom, a family personal assistant developed from Min
Tao's six module project plans.

2
00:00:05,978 --> 00:00:09,143
This walkthrough shows screenshots captured from the working application.

3
00:00:09,143 --> 00:00:10,901
All family records are synthetic.

4
00:00:10,901 --> 00:00:17,583
The default demonstration uses deterministic specialist roles and does not
call a language model or connect to real accounts.

5
00:00:17,583 --> 00:00:26,374
The problem is familiar: a schedule change arrives in one app, a class
reminder arrives in another, and somehow a parent becomes the integration
layer.

6
00:00:26,374 --> 00:00:28,836
I wanted to reduce that mental work.

7
00:00:28,836 --> 00:00:34,814
The application separates six responsibilities: coordination, information
retrieval, weekly planning, independent criticism, longer-term student
planning, and reflection.

8
00:00:34,814 --> 00:00:42,550
These roles exchange structured case records, so I can see where an
assumption entered the workflow and which check still needs attention.

9
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:46,426
The example replays Thursday, August thirteenth, twenty twenty-six.

10
00:00:46,426 --> 00:00:49,771
The source view preserves the original soccer notice as superseded.

11
00:00:49,771 --> 00:00:54,120
The current BYGA update moves practice to five thirty through seven P M.

12
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:57,130
LingoAce still shows Chinese class from six to seven.

13
00:00:57,130 --> 00:01:00,141
Each record retains its identity, revision, and retrieval time.

14
00:01:00,141 --> 00:01:05,158
Keeping both versions matters because the older message can still look
relevant in a search.

15
00:01:05,158 --> 00:01:07,834
Relevance alone does not make a record authoritative.

16
00:01:07,834 --> 00:01:12,517
The event identifier connects the versions, while revision and status
determine which notice applies.

17
00:01:12,517 --> 00:01:15,862
The source view also shows the affected child and location.

18
00:01:15,862 --> 00:01:21,883
If those details are unclear, the assistant needs clarification before
treating the event as a reliable scheduling fact.

19
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:27,138
The Information Agent ranks three records using text vectors and latent
semantic retrieval.

20
00:01:27,138 --> 00:01:30,256
Current-record validation excludes the old notice from the active schedule.

21
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:33,687
Deterministic time checks find a sixty-minute overlap for the same child.

22
00:01:33,687 --> 00:01:37,118
The response cites the records and saves an observable case trace.

23
00:01:37,118 --> 00:01:39,613
A missing source would keep this check pending.

24
00:01:39,613 --> 00:01:41,796
Retrieval and conflict detection do different jobs.

25
00:01:41,796 --> 00:01:43,979
Retrieval finds useful evidence for the question.

26
00:01:43,979 --> 00:01:48,969
The scheduling check compares actual dates and times across the current
records in the loaded dataset.

27
00:01:48,969 --> 00:01:53,335
It does not rely on a language model to estimate whether two intervals
overlap.

28
00:01:53,335 --> 00:01:56,142
Here, both activities include six to seven P M.

29
00:01:56,142 --> 00:02:00,508
Showing that evidence makes the answer easy for a parent to inspect and
correct.

30
00:02:01,708 --> 00:02:03,775
The Planning Agent compares structured alternatives.

31
00:02:03,775 --> 00:02:09,285
A separate Schedule Critic checks evidence, group commitments, and the
assumed thirty-minute travel buffer before scoring.

32
00:02:09,285 --> 00:02:14,796
The confirmed Friday Chinese make-up resolves the example conflict and
scores ninety-seven out of one hundred.

33
00:02:14,796 --> 00:02:17,895
The search has explicit branching, depth, and time limits.

34
00:02:17,895 --> 00:02:20,306
Unsupported options remain pending or are rejected.

35
00:02:20,306 --> 00:02:27,539
The planner can generate up to four alternatives at a node, retain three
states, and search to a depth of three.

36
00:02:27,539 --> 00:02:30,294
It also limits expansion count and search time.

37
00:02:30,294 --> 00:02:34,771
Those boundaries keep a difficult scheduling question from turning into an
endless search.

38
00:02:34,771 --> 00:02:38,904
The critic considers feasibility, current evidence, protected commitments,
disruption, transportation, and clarity.

39
00:02:38,904 --> 00:02:43,726
The thirty-minute travel allowance is a conservative prototype assumption,
not a live traffic estimate.

40
00:02:43,726 --> 00:02:49,925
A make-up slot must appear in the evidence before the planner can treat it
as an available solution.

41
00:02:51,125 --> 00:02:54,153
Here I tried to execute the proposed change without approval.

42
00:02:54,153 --> 00:02:55,364
The application rejected it.

43
00:02:55,364 --> 00:02:58,694
An approval covers the exact action and expires after ten minutes.

44
00:02:58,694 --> 00:03:02,932
The server also rejects a changed payload, changed source evidence, or a
reused approval.

45
00:03:02,932 --> 00:03:06,263
Model commentary and instructions inside a notice cannot grant this
permission.

46
00:03:06,263 --> 00:03:09,290
This is more than a confirmation message on a screen.

47
00:03:09,290 --> 00:03:12,318
The server enforces the rule where the effect would happen.

48
00:03:12,318 --> 00:03:17,162
A recommendation can be useful without giving the assistant permission to
commit the family to it.

49
00:03:17,162 --> 00:03:19,584
The preview names the event and proposed times.

50
00:03:19,584 --> 00:03:23,520
If the underlying schedule changes before execution, the old approval no
longer applies.

51
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:27,758
I have to review a fresh plan rather than unknowingly approve a stale one.

52
00:03:28,958 --> 00:03:36,578
After I approve the exact action, the application writes the change to the
local demonstration calendar and reads it back to verify success.

53
00:03:36,578 --> 00:03:39,559
The approval and execution remain in the audit trail.

54
00:03:39,559 --> 00:03:43,535
This demonstration does not book the LingoAce make-up or update Google
Calendar.

55
00:03:43,535 --> 00:03:45,523
The original provider records remain unchanged.

56
00:03:45,523 --> 00:03:49,498
The distinction between a proposed change and a verified result is
important.

57
00:03:49,498 --> 00:03:54,467
A tool call might fail, return an unexpected response, or succeed without
the interface noticing.

58
00:03:54,467 --> 00:03:59,105
The local workflow records the effect and checks the saved state before
reporting success.

59
00:03:59,105 --> 00:04:03,412
In a future live integration, each provider will need its own equivalent
verification.

60
00:04:03,412 --> 00:04:08,050
Until that exists, the application describes this outcome explicitly as a
local demonstration effect.

61
00:04:09,250 --> 00:04:12,006
The simulated outbox creates a family follow-up task.

62
00:04:12,006 --> 00:04:14,761
Repeating the notification does not send a duplicate.

63
00:04:14,761 --> 00:04:19,583
I can acknowledge the task, mark it done, snooze it, or report a correction.

64
00:04:19,583 --> 00:04:21,650
Completed feedback survives a browser reload.

65
00:04:21,650 --> 00:04:25,783
The assistant uses persistent SQLite memory to carry this state between
visits.

66
00:04:25,783 --> 00:04:29,572
Memory is what makes the assistant useful beyond a single answer.

67
00:04:29,572 --> 00:04:34,050
It records whether a task is pending, acknowledged, completed, snoozed,
incorrect, or rescheduled.

68
00:04:34,050 --> 00:04:37,839
A snoozed task can produce one reminder after the delay expires.

69
00:04:37,839 --> 00:04:40,250
Completing a task stops that reminder path.

70
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:41,972
Quiet hours defer notifications overnight.

71
00:04:41,972 --> 00:04:49,550
These controls matter because an assistant that repeatedly tells me what I
already know would simply become one more thing to manage.

72
00:04:50,750 --> 00:04:52,231
Now the LingoAce check fails.

73
00:04:52,231 --> 00:04:57,266
The assistant reports that the check is incomplete, keeps the decision
pending, and removes the notification action.

74
00:04:57,266 --> 00:05:01,412
It does not turn unavailable information into a claim that the schedule is
clear.

75
00:05:01,412 --> 00:05:04,077
This failure scenario is part of the regression suite.

76
00:05:04,077 --> 00:05:08,520
This is also how I approach a school notice that only contains a protected
link.

77
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:12,074
Without authorized access to the details, the item has not been reviewed.

78
00:05:12,074 --> 00:05:16,220
The assistant should not invent the missing date or assume that nothing
needs doing.

79
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:20,070
The prototype includes separate scenarios for an unknown child and
conflicting source records.

80
00:05:20,070 --> 00:05:24,217
Each one returns an unresolved state that a parent can recognize and act on.

81
00:05:25,417 --> 00:05:28,061
The tournament scenario demonstrates a hard family rule.

82
00:05:28,061 --> 00:05:31,366
Skipping a soccer tournament requires a separate parent-provided illness
decision.

83
00:05:31,366 --> 00:05:34,671
The prototype never infers illness, so it rejects this branch.

84
00:05:34,671 --> 00:05:36,984
A numerical score cannot override the rule.

85
00:05:36,984 --> 00:05:38,967
Unresolved choices return to the parent.

86
00:05:38,967 --> 00:05:42,603
Family priorities are not always reducible to a convenient numerical score.

87
00:05:42,603 --> 00:05:45,577
Group activities and commitments without make-up options deserve protection.

88
00:05:45,577 --> 00:05:50,204
Sometimes both commitments are important and the rules do not select a clear
winner.

89
00:05:50,204 --> 00:05:52,848
That is a legitimate stopping point for automation.

90
00:05:52,848 --> 00:05:58,467
The assistant's job is to make the trade-off visible and give the parent
enough context to decide.

91
00:05:59,667 --> 00:06:03,211
The High School and College Advisor provides a four-year discussion
template.

92
00:06:03,211 --> 00:06:07,401
It keeps school-specific requirements and dates unverified until current
official sources are supplied.

93
00:06:07,401 --> 00:06:09,334
Parent and student review are required.

94
00:06:09,334 --> 00:06:12,879
The assistant does not predict admission or replace the school counselor.

95
00:06:12,879 --> 00:06:16,746
This role works on a different time horizon from the weekly scheduler.

96
00:06:16,746 --> 00:06:22,868
A ninth-grade discussion might begin with interests and course choices,
while later years introduce campus research and application milestones.

97
00:06:22,868 --> 00:06:26,413
Those are planning topics, not verified requirements for a particular
school.

98
00:06:26,413 --> 00:06:29,313
The student also needs a voice in the plan.

99
00:06:29,313 --> 00:06:35,758
The assistant can organize questions for a counselor meeting without
pretending to know what is best for the student's future.

100
00:06:36,958 --> 00:06:41,358
The Reflection Agent summarizes saved cases, completed tasks, and verified
local actions.

101
00:06:41,358 --> 00:06:45,758
Forty-one automated tests pass, and the browser walkthrough checks the real
interface.

102
00:06:45,758 --> 00:06:49,792
These are small synthetic tests, not proof of live service reliability.

103
00:06:49,792 --> 00:06:54,192
The GitHub-ready package includes the code, project plan, report, and
reproduction scripts.

104
00:06:54,192 --> 00:06:59,325
The next stage is an authorized pilot with real accounts and representative
evaluation data.

105
00:06:59,325 --> 00:07:01,525
The evaluation includes nine demonstration scenarios.

106
00:07:01,525 --> 00:07:08,492
Five authored cases are used for the binary conflict calculation, with four
detected conflicts and one correctly clear schedule.

107
00:07:08,492 --> 00:07:12,892
That small result supports a regression check, not a broad accuracy claim.

108
00:07:12,892 --> 00:07:18,758
The browser test also exercises approval, saved feedback, and the failure
path through the actual interface.

109
00:07:18,758 --> 00:07:24,992
Before personal use, I still need representative notice extraction tests,
complete source synchronization, and live delivery checks.

110
00:07:24,992 --> 00:07:31,592
The code and report make those remaining steps explicit so the next phase
can build on measured behavior.

111
00:07:32,792 --> 00:07:36,987
Just as I was finishing this project, Meta released Muse, its own personal
AI agent.

112
00:07:36,987 --> 00:07:40,342
Apparently, my capstone now has a competitor with a slightly bigger budget.

113
00:07:40,342 --> 00:07:42,020
So much for my head start!

114
00:07:42,020 --> 00:07:47,893
But the timing does make a point: mom or not, we could all use a little help
with the mental juggling.

115
00:07:47,893 --> 00:07:55,724
A good personal assistant should help us feel more organized and less
overwhelmed, so we can give our limited attention to the people and
experiences that matter most.

116
00:07:55,724 --> 00:07:58,800
And maybe, just once, drink our coffee while it's still hot.
